{
  "_": "money's screenshots (.github/screens/apps.md; which phones it is on is flake.nix's list, `publish`): its server is server.sh, seeded up to the run's day (DEMO_DAY), signed in to as `user`, who goes by `name`; every phone and tablet signs in to it, so each shows one household on one day. The app opened once for each device and theme and every shot taken in that one launch, in order: each of `screens` that is `on` the device, by its launch arguments as a launch link (`links`: the shell puts back what it showed, then opens that screen, as a launch would). A screen's `route` is its address, which every shell takes as the same launch (money_app's `ShellMsg::Address`, held to its `args` by `every_shot_route_is_its_launch`): a driver should open the `route` alone where there is one, not the arguments and then the route. `desktop` is the iced window's (ui/rust/shots): its size, and its shots, each clicking what a text on the screen says, in one window. Its accounts are Checking's register, its transactions all accounts'. `welcome`, the first run's pages (its route, welcome/), is the last of `screens`, `fresh`: what it leaves up is no place for a launch link (taken before the screens, on Android the next link was lost under the pages and a category came out as `budget`).",
