  "_screens": "`screens`: one list, each screen opened by its launch arguments alone (ark_app::shell::Launch: .github/screens/apps.md) on the devices it is `on`, under one id on all of them. The phones (`ios`, `android`) and the larger screens (`ipad-portrait`, `ipad-landscape`, `android-tablet`, `fold-unfolded`, `fold-folded`) take the same screens in the same order: the budget, a category, the accounts, an account's register, To Review, a transaction (the newest with a receipt), a new transaction, Insights, Settings, the budget's Auto-Assign menu, then the first run's pages. A category and a transaction are two entries, one id: on the larger screens in the inspector (`-inspector 1`), on a phone as the platform shows them (Category Details, the transaction's form). The Mac (`mac`) takes them too but for the menu and the pages: it has no step driver and no fresh launch, and no browser to sign it in, so `launch.mac` opens the demo's household before each (at 1440x900), on the run's day (app-mac.sh gives `-demo` DEMO_DAY), the same household the server is seeded with.",
  "launch": {
    "mac": [
      "-demo",
      "2026-11-18",
      "-window",
      "1440x900",
      "-ApplePersistenceIgnoreState",
      "YES"
    ]
  },
  "screens": [
